         Prior build - 1.0.17.0
         (The unload error: a contended config save on the shared Dalamud database escaping Dispose):
         Reported: "Sometimes on one of the clients will get an unload error."
         Found in the log rather than guessed - [ERR] [LocalPlugin] Error while unloading
         BozjaBuddyReborn, and the inner exception is SQLite.SQLiteException: database is locked,
         thrown out of SavePluginConfig at the last line of Plugin.Dispose.

         WHY IT IS A MULTIBOX PROBLEM SPECIFICALLY. Dalamud does not write plugin configs straight
         to disk: SavePluginConfig goes through ReliableFileStorage, which is a SQLite database
         inside the XIVLauncher folder - and every client running off one XIVLauncher installation
         shares that single database. With four boxes, two clients saving in the same moment is
         routine, and the loser gets the lock error. Dalamud's own DiscordBridge is visible in the
         same log hitting the identical error on the identical call, so this is contention, not
         corruption.
         Uncaught in Dispose, a lost config write is promoted into an UNLOAD FAILURE: Dalamud then
         warns that the plugin may be in an inconsistent state and the game should be restarted.
         That is an enormously worse outcome than not persisting one setting.

         Every save now goes through ConfigSaver, which retries a couple of times - the lock is
         held for milliseconds while another client finishes its transaction, so the retry almost
         always lands - and then gives up quietly with one Information-level line naming the real
         cause. Settings re-save on the next change anyway. Applied to all fourteen save sites, not
         just the one in Dispose, because the same contention can throw out of an ImGui draw or the
         framework tick just as easily; those would have surfaced as a mid-session crash instead.
         Compile-verified Debug and Release (0 warnings).
         SEAM (in-game): the retry count and 20ms spacing are judgement calls tuned to "another
         client is mid-transaction", not measured. If the warning still appears often, the honest
         next step is to stop saving from Dispose at all and rely on the save that already happens
         on every settings change.

