         Prior build - 1.0.15.0
         (Every duty-action slot read empty, on every box including your own):
         Reported: "The actions are empty for all even myself even though we have actions."
         TWO INDEPENDENT CAUSES, either of which alone was enough to empty the whole bar.

         (1) A CIRCULAR GATE. DutyActionSync.Tick read `Available = DutyActions.Available;` and
         then only called ReadBoth() `if (Available)` - but Available is a flag that ReadBoth is
         what SETS. It starts false, so the read never ran, so the flag never became true, so the
         read never ran. Nothing was ever read on any box, and since the wire faithfully carried
         those empty slots to everyone else, every row on every client showed empty too. The read
         is now unconditional and the flag simply reports what it found.

         (2) THE WRONG "IS THERE ANYTHING HERE" TEST, and a fragile way of getting at the data.
         The read required DutyActionManager.ActionsPresent, but that flag mirrors the UI state
         (its own comment points at RaptureHotbarModule.SetDutyActionsPresent) rather than whether
         actions are loaded - so it can be false with a fully populated duty bar on screen. An
         action id of zero is the real "nothing here", and that is the test now.
         The manager was also fetched through DutyActionManager.GetInstanceIfReady(), a standalone
         signature-scanned function: when a signature goes stale it returns null silently, which
         presents as exactly this bug. Bozja's slots do not live on BozjaState at all - that holds
         only the holster, the stock of actions you OWN - they live on the content director, as
         ContentDirector.DutyActionManager, and PublicContentBozja inherits ContentDirector. So
         the manager is now taken from the director this plugin already reads mettle and the
         holster from, by explicit-layout cast, needing no extra signature; GetInstanceIfReady is
         the second choice, and the UI's own RaptureHotbarModule.GetDutyActionSlot (with charges
         and recast from ActionManager) is the third, answering even when no director is reachable.

         AND IT NOW EXPLAINS ITSELF. DutyActions.Diagnostic records which source answered and what
         it saw - slot count, the ActionsPresent flag, or the specific failure - and the window
         prints it whenever the bar reads empty. A bar showing nothing while actions are plainly on
         screen is a read problem rather than a game state, and that difference should be visible
         instead of guessable.
         Compile-verified Debug and Release (0 warnings).
         SEAM (in-game): which of the three sources actually answers in Bozja is the thing to
         report back - the window names it. If the bar is still empty, that line says why.

         Prior build - 1.0.14.0
         (Shared duty-action hotbar across every multibox client, Occult-Crescent style):
         Requested: a duty action hotbar like Phantom Jobs in Occult Crescent, showing what each
