         Prior build - 1.0.3.0
         (Travel: actually mount, and stop handing vnavmesh flight paths a grounded character cannot follow; plus a work-zone picker):
         Two things, one of them a real defect.
         (1) THE PLUGIN NEVER MOUNTED. vnavmesh has no mount IPC - summoning a mount is the
         orchestrator's job and it was simply missing, so the character jogged the entire map on
         foot. Worse, Movement passed fly:AllowFlight unconditionally; handing vnavmesh a 3D
         flight path while the character is grounded and unmounted gives it a route it physically
         cannot follow and it stalls partway. New Automation/Mount.cs mounts past 30y (Mount
         Roulette, GeneralAction 9 - verified against GeneralAction.csv), passes the ACTUAL
         airborne state (ConditionFlag.InFlight) as the fly flag, and dismounts (GeneralAction 23)
         before combat. The controller now refuses to arm RSR until grounded, because you cannot
         attack from a mount and arming early just looks like "RSR is doing nothing".
         Established while investigating the request for teleporting: neither Bozja nor Zadnor has
         a single row in the Aetheryte sheet, so there is NO in-zone teleport network of any kind.
         Mount travel is the fast travel; there is nothing faster to reach for.
         (2) WORK-ZONE PICKER next to Start: Anywhere / Z1 / Z2 / Z3. Stores the number so one
         choice carries across both field zones, with labels adapting to the zone you are in. A
         selected farm material takes precedence (it pins region AND activity) and the picker
